9. What problem are you trying to solve, and why is it important?
-Contemporary technological advancements often contribute to a sedentary lifestyle, with individuals spending extended periods engaged with screens, leading to detrimental health effects associated with inactivity. Furthermore, many fitness applications fail to offer real-time feedback, limiting their ability to provide personalized guidance. In addition, these platforms often lack meaningful social interaction, which could otherwise enhance user engagement and motivation.

10. What is your proposed solution?
-Leveraging our low-code SDK, developers can seamlessly create motion-controlled games that promote physical activity while integrating blockchain-based rewards and social elements. Our advanced computer vision technology ensures real-time feedback, guiding users to perform exercises with precision and maximizing their effectiveness. By embedding these features on the Aptos blockchain, we provide a decentralized, secure platform for users to track progress, engage in tournaments, and connect with a like-minded fitness community, driving deeper user engagement and fostering a thriving Web3 fitness ecosystem.

